menu "LispBM REPL"
    config LISP_REPL_ENABLE
        bool "Enable RAM-only LispBM UART REPL and LCD terminal"
        depends on BOARD_DISPLAY_ENABLE && BOARD_WROVER_KIT_V41_CONFIRMED && SPIRAM
        default n
        help
            Experimental, opt-in. Uses UART0/115200 and the confirmed LCD.
            Lisp state and the upstream image are RAM-only. No NVS, filesystem,
            Bluetooth, DSP or GPIO extensions. Ctrl-C resets the Lisp environment.
            Requires a separately installed pinned LispBM checkout (GPLv3+).
    config LISP_APP_ENABLE
        bool "Enable one foreground Lisp application with a full-screen canvas"
        depends on LISP_REPL_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            Opt-in, RAM-only callbacks and two fixed PSRAM RGB565 canvases
            (300 KiB). Original Lisp and LCD tasks retain sole ownership.
            UART Ctrl-C stops the app; TCP :stop and :key X remain available.
            No filesystem, persistent loader, GPIO, Bluetooth or DSP.
    config WIFI_REPL_ENABLE
        bool "Enable plain TCP REPL on port2323 (no TLS/token)"
        depends on LISP_REPL_ENABLE && WIFI_SERVICE_CONNECT_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            No certificate, token or login. Anyone on the reachable LAN can
            execute RAM-only Lisp; use only on a trusted LAN, never public.
            Connect with nc DEVICE_IP 2323. One client, original Lisp owner and
            LCD output. OTA keeps its separate HTTPS certificate and token.
endmenu
